KG42.register("clusters-e7316d19f17de9799cfb033c",{"id":"44-blockchain_phev_trading::v142-d-K003","paper":"44-blockchain_phev_trading","label":"Qualitative role selection of the charging buyer","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-K003","label":"Qualitative role selection of the charging buyer","market_meaning":"A PHEV selects the charging role according to its current energy state and driving plan, and participates in PETCON transactions as a local electric-energy buyer in the capacity of a charging PHEV. This cluster expresses only the qualitative role selection and the buyer's participation capability, and does not claim to cover complete admission or all role decisions.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M01"],"market_types":["LEM"],"process_stages":["participation"],"scope_disposition":"compatible","scope_explanation":"Role selection and the charging-PHEV buyer identity are both situated in the local PHEV participation context of the same mechanism. The statement that no trusted third party for transactions is needed is understood only in terms of the transaction arrangement and is not interpreted as requiring no registration authority. The efficiency, bids, or clearing thresholds of other chains are not added to the role-selection conditions.","assembly_status":"assembled","boundary_rationale":"The current energy state and driving plan constitute the basis for the qualitative selection, the PHEV is the selecting subject, and the charging-buyer identity is the result, which has independent market meaning. A single chain can already express the candidate rule of this limited scope; complete identity admission and the mutual-exclusion relationships of all roles belong to an extension scope not yet covered.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R007","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Fully retain the two clauses of charging-buyer participation and qualitative role selection, and do not fabricate selection thresholds from parameters or nodes of other functions."}],"connections":[],"object_mappings":[],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-K003-G01","category":"unverified_source","description":"The evidence in this cluster concerning role selection, buyer identity, and third-party transaction arrangements remains unverified; assembled means only candidate semantic assembly within a limited scope.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R007"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C001","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e002","v141-b-g03-E03","v141-b-g03-E08"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"In subsequent work, check the source scope of the roles and transaction arrangements; the status of this cluster must not be interpreted as independent confirmation of the sources or participation eligibility."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K003-G02","category":"ontology_extension","description":"Current C does not cover trusted-authority registration, certificates, or initialization conditions; the registration-admission proposal is still pending. The absence of a need for a trusted transaction third party and the need for a registration authority are not mutually substitutable participation conditions.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R007"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C001","v141-c-R007::V::participation.consumer"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e018","v141-b-g01-e019","v141-b-g03-E08"],"proposal_ids":["v141-b-g01-p002"],"required_work":"If it is extended into a complete participation-admission rule, the registration-admission proposal should first be handled by a human, and then upstream should preserve the registration and initialization rule chain; the currently limited role-selection scope does not add admission nodes on this basis."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K003-G03","category":"upstream_missing","description":"The existing chain carries only the charging-buyer function and does not separately represent the discharging role, the idle role, or a complete state-to-role mapping. The three-role narrative cannot be directly rewritten in D as mutually exclusive or exactly-one graph constraints.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R007"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e002","v141-b-g01-e039"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"If a complete role-decision mechanism is needed, upstream is to supplement the other roles and their applicability relationships according to the source; this cluster continues to express only the qualitative selection of the charging buyer and does not add thresholds or mutual-exclusion edges."}]},"rule_refs":["44-blockchain_phev_trading::v141-c-R007"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-fc2134ec5ed3e3df"]});
